Reading:
- Every one of the 10 cells is missing exactly the eliminated
  `capture:nested/root-member/N` cuts (and, for updateMany, the eliminated
  `admit:nested-member/N` cuts) — nothing else. `admit:nested-template` and
  `admit:nested-template/root-member/N` still fire, once per root member, for
  both shapes.
- No cell's outcome KIND differs from `recipe.outcome`: the three
  "TransactionError ... could not read back" observations are the
  recipe's OWN `missingTerminalRow: true` design (the seed data chains each
  root's `parentId` into another root, so one root's nested deleteMany
  deletes a row the outer updateMany's own RETURNING still expects back) —
  not a new failure kind introduced by U6.2. No cell needed the "outcome
  differs in kind" branch of the brief (U1 empty-filter admission / D-29
  premise ordering); every cell's `observation.outcome.kind` already matched
  `recipe.outcome === "success" ? "success" : "failure"`.
- `nestedAdmission` (the `admitNestedMember` call count) is exactly
  `rootCount + 1` for both shapes now (1 template admission + 1 per root
  member); it is no longer `rootCount*2+1` for updateMany, because the second,
  per-captured-member re-admission pass no longer runs.
- `recordSeriesProgress.{committedSegments,committedWriteMembers,completedMembers}`
  on the atomic-batch `missing-terminal-row` deleteMany cells is exactly
  `rootCount` (2 for the two rootCount=2 seeds, 4 for the rootCount=4 seed),
  not the old `rootCount*2-1` — a written root member (its own write plus its
  now-one-statement nested set) is one progress unit, not two.
